---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";

// Every factual claim below is deliberately unquantified. Tree counts,
// hectares, dates, species and partner organisations are left out rather
// than estimated — an invented number is precisely what makes an
// environmental page worthless. Fill these in once they're confirmed.
---
<Layout
  title="Environmental work"
  description="What DST actually does about the environment: conifer planting in the Urals, work starting in Yerevan, and an open search for environmental contacts in Dubai."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Environment</p>
    <h1>What we actually do about the environment</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most company pages under this heading are a stock photograph of a leaf
      and a paragraph about caring deeply. This one is a list of things that
      have either happened or are being worked on, with the ones that
      haven't happened yet labelled as such.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" id="urals">
    <h2>Conifer planting in the Urals</h2>
    <p>
      The part of this with the longest history: planting coniferous trees in
      the Urals. It grew out of the personal background of the people behind
      DST rather than a corporate initiative — which is also why it predates
      the company and isn't structured as a programme with a reporting cycle.
    </p>
    <p>
      Conifers are the sensible choice for that region for reasons worth
      stating plainly: they're native to it, they survive the winters without
      intervention, and they hold soil on ground that would otherwise erode.
      A planting suited to its site needs no maintenance budget to stay
      alive — which is what separates reforestation that lasts from the kind
      that photographs well in year one and is gone by year five.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" id="next">
    <h2>What's being worked on now</h2>

    <h3>Yerevan</h3>
    <p>
      The intention is to take part in environmental work in Yerevan and —
      just as importantly — to document it properly, so there's a record
      rather than a claim. Nothing is finished here yet. When it is, this
      section will say what was done and when.
    </p>

    <h3>Dubai</h3>
    <p>
      Dubai is where DST operates day to day, and it's where we have the
      fewest environmental contacts. That's the honest state of it. We're
      looking for organisations, initiatives and people already doing
      credible environmental work in the UAE — not to sponsor a logo
      placement, but to find something worth actually taking part in.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you run something along those lines, or know someone who does, the
      contact details are at the bottom of this page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout>
    Nothing on this page is an offset. DST doesn't sell carbon credits,
    doesn't count any of this against its own footprint, and makes no
    neutrality claim. It's work we do because we want to, described as
    plainly as we can manage.
  </Callout>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Why this sits on its own site</h2>
    <p>
      Environmental work kept as a tab on a commercial site tends to read as
      decoration for the commercial part. Its own domain lets it stay small
      and specific without having to justify itself against a sales page —
      and lets this page admit that two of the three things on it haven't
      happened yet, which a marketing page would never do.
    </p>
    <p>
      DST's commercial work — real estate, company formation, and the rest —
      lives at <a href="https://dst.llc" title="DST — the group's main site">dst.llc</a>.
      It is deliberately not cross-sold from here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container" id="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Updates and photographs from the plantings go to Instagram, which is
      the most honest format for this: dated posts, in order, rather than a
      curated summary written after the fact.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://www.instagram.com/eco.dst.llc/" rel="me noopener" title="DST Eco on Instagram">@eco.dst.llc on Instagram</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      For anything else — particularly environmental contacts in Dubai —
      reach us through <a href="https://dst.llc" title="DST — contact">dst.llc</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
